SUMMARY:Ali Wong Live at Neal S Blaisdell Concert Hall (Friday)
DTSTAMP:20260720T113558Z
DTSTART:20260724T190000Z
DESCRIPTION:Official TicketsResale Tickets \nThis post contains affiliate l
	inks. We may earn a commission at no extra cost to you. \nAbout the Perfor
	mer\nAli Wong is one of the most celebrated stand-up comedians of her gene
	ration. Known for her fearless\, raw\, and unapologetically honest humor\,
	 she burst into mainstream consciousness with her Netflix specials Baby Co
	bra (2016) and Hard Knock Wife (2018)\, both filmed while she was visibly 
	pregnant — a bold comedic choice that became her signature. \nHer comedy d
	ives deep into marriage\, motherhood\, sex\, and the immigrant experience 
	with a sharp wit and zero filter. She has since starred in the Netflix rom
	antic comedy film Always Be My Maybe (2019)\, which she co-wrote\, and the
	 critically acclaimed Hulu series Beef (2023)\, for which she won an Emmy 
	Award. Ali Wong is a true force in comedy — and her live shows are legenda
	ry for their energy and intimacy. \nFans can expect a night of bold\, boun
	dary-pushing stand-up that is both hilarious and deeply personal. Ali Wong
	’s live performances are known for their electric atmosphere and her abili
	ty to connect with audiences on a profound level. \nEvent Details\n\nDate:
	 Friday\, July 24\, 2026\nTime: 7:00 PM HST (Doors open earlier)\nVenue: N
	eal S Blaisdell Concert Hall\, 777 Ward Avenue\, Honolulu\, HI 96814\nShow
	 Duration: Approximately 90 minutes\nAge Restrictions: All ages welcome\n\
	nAbout the Venue\nThe Neal S Blaisdell Concert Hall is Honolulu’s premier 
	performing arts venue\, located at 777 Ward Avenue in the heart of the cit
	y. Part of the Blaisdell Center complex\, the Concert Hall seats approxima
	tely 2\,158 guests and is renowned for its excellent acoustics and intimat
	e atmosphere despite its size. \nThe venue features comfortable theater-st
	yle seating\, multiple concession areas\, and easy access to parking in th
	e adjacent Blaisdell Center parking structure. The surrounding area offers
	 a variety of dining and entertainment options\, making it easy to turn th
	e evening into a full night out in Honolulu. \nThe Blaisdell Concert Hall 
	has hosted some of the world’s biggest names in entertainment\, from class
	ical orchestras to top-tier comedians. Its central location makes it easil
	y accessible from Waikiki and downtown Honolulu\, and valet parking is ava
	ilable for added convenience. \nWhat to Expect\nAli Wong’s live show is a 
	solo stand-up performance — no opening acts\, just Ali on stage delivering
	 her signature brand of comedy for approximately 90 minutes. Expect a high
	-energy\, laugh-out-loud evening filled with stories about her life\, rela
	tionships\, and observations on modern culture. \nHer Honolulu shows are e
	specially anticipated given her Hawaiian roots and connection to the islan
	ds. The July 24 show is the first of two nights at the Blaisdell — the sec
	ond show (July 25) was added after the first sold out quickly\, a testamen
	t to her massive popularity in Hawaii. \nArrive early to find your seats a
	nd enjoy the venue’s amenities. This is a must-see event for comedy fans i
	n Honolulu. \nTicket Information\nPrice Range: $54.50 – $127+ (resale pric
	es may vary) \nPurchase official tickets directly through Ticketmaster\, o
	r find resale tickets through VividSeats for flexible options including pa
	irs and premium seating. \nOfficial TicketsResale Tickets \nThis post cont
	ains affiliate links. We may earn a commission at no extra cost to you.\n\
	nhttps://comedycalendar.com/event/ali-wong-live-at-neal-s-blaisdell-concer
	t-hall-friday/\n\nFrom Comedy Calendar
